    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-public-health-contact-information-act-2020-sch-1-sec-94c-ss-5",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "94C(5) Constitutional basis of this Part",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-public-health-contact-information-act-2020#sch-1-sec-94c-ss-5"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-amendment-public-health-contact-information-act-2020.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-public-health-contact-information-act-2020.pdf, p.10",
      "values:originalText": "(5) This Part also has effect as if it were expressly confined to giving\neffect to Australia’s obligations under the International Covenant\non Civil and Political Rights done at New York on 16 December\n1966 ([1980] ATS 23), and in particular Article 17 of the\nCovenant, in relation to COVID app data.\nNote:\nThe Covenant is set out in Australian Treaty Series 1980 No. 23\n([1980] ATS 23) and could in 2020 be viewed in the Australian\nTreaties Library on the AustLII website (www.austlii.edu.au).",
      "skos:definition": "(5) This Part also has effect as if it were expressly confined to giving\neffect to Australia’s obligations under the International Covenant\non Civil and Political Rights done at New York on 16 December\n1966 ([1980] ATS 23), and in particular Article 17 of the\nCovenant, in relation to COVID app data.\nNote:\nThe Covenant is set out in Australian Treaty Series 1980 No. 23\n([1980] ATS 23) and could in 2020 be viewed in the Australian\nTreaties Library on the AustLII website (www.austlii.edu.au).",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-public-health-contact-information-act-2020-sch-1-sec-94c"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-public-health-contact-information-act-2020-sch-1-sec-94c-ss-5-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-public-health-contact-information-act-2020-sch-1-sec-94c-ss-5-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "4d5078b6952fcc41915681858aef7b0d507630a9a70cfd71a294dc77643bea55",
      "skos:note": "Australia's obligations under the International Covenant on Civil and Political Rights"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-public-health-contact-information-act-2020#sch-1-sec-94c-ss-5",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "94C(5) Constitutional basis of this Part",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 10,
      "values:originalText": "(5) This Part also has effect as if it were expressly confined to giving\neffect to Australia’s obligations under the International Covenant\non Civil and Political Rights done at New York on 16 December\n1966 ([1980] ATS 23), and in particular Article 17 of the\nCovenant, in relation to COVID app data.\nNote:\nThe Covenant is set out in Australian Treaty Series 1980 No. 23\n([1980] ATS 23) and could in 2020 be viewed in the Australian\nTreaties Library on the AustLII website (www.austlii.edu.au)."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-public-health-contact-information-act-2020-sch-1-sec-94c-ss-5-norm",
