        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-public-health-contact-information-act-2020-sch-1-sec-94d-ss-3-logic-ltl-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-public-health-contact-information-act-2020-sch-1-sec-94d-ss-3-logic-deontic-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-public-health-contact-information-act-2020-sch-1-sec-94d-ss-3-logic-deontic-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-public-health-contact-information-act-2020-sch-1-sec-94d-ss-3-logic-deontic-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "1ead17c54656f6cf2ffb4bb720a9258d7fb4ba1f9ff566654076fed94b8c7e23",
      "skos:note": "Permitted collection of COVID app data under Australian law."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-public-health-contact-information-act-2020#sch-1-sec-94d-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "94D(3) Collection, use or disclosure of COVID app data",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 10,
      "values:originalText": "(3) Subsection (1) does not apply to the collection of COVID app data\nif:\n\n(a) the collection of the COVID app data:\n\n(i) occurs as part of the collection, at the same time, of data\nthat is not COVID app data (non-COVID app data);\nand\n\n(ii) is incidental to the collection of the non-COVID app\ndata; and\n\n(b) the collection of the non-COVID app data is permitted under\nan Australian law; and\n\n(c) the COVID app data:\n\n(i) is deleted as soon as practicable after the person\nbecomes aware that it had been collected; and\n\n(ii) is not otherwise accessed, used or disclosed by the\nperson after it was collected.\nNote:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matters in\nthis subsection: see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code."
    },
