      "cml:conclusionText": "Person is a former COVIDSafe user"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-public-health-contact-information-act-2020-sch-1-sec-94p",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "94P Obligations after the end of the COVIDSafe data period",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-public-health-contact-information-act-2020#sch-1-sec-94p"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-amendment-public-health-contact-information-act-2020.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-public-health-contact-information-act-2020.pdf, p.18",
      "values:originalText": "(1) After the end of the day determined under subsection 94Y(1), the\ndata store administrator must not:\n\n(a) collect any COVID app data; or\n\n(b) make COVIDSafe available to be downloaded.\n\n(2) As soon as reasonably practicable after the end of the day\ndetermined under subsection 94Y(1), the data store administrator\nmust delete all COVID app data from the National COVIDSafe\nData Store.\n\n(3) As soon as reasonably practicable after the deletion, the data store\nadministrator must:\n\n(a) inform the Health Minister and the Commissioner that all\nCOVID app data has been deleted from the National\nCOVIDSafe Data Store; and\n\n(b) take all reasonable steps to inform all COVIDSafe users\n(other than former COVIDSafe users) in relation to\ncommunication devices that:\n\n(i) all COVID app data has been deleted from the National\nCOVIDSafe Data Store; and\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\n\nNo. 44, 2020\nPrivacy Amendment (Public Health Contact Information) Act 2020\n\n(ii) COVID app data can no longer be collected; and\n\n(iii) they should delete COVIDSafe from their\ncommunication devices.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) After the end of the day determined under subsection 94Y(1), the\ndata store administrator must not:\n\n(a) collect any COVID app data; or\n\n(b) make COVIDSafe available to be downloaded.\n\n(2) As soon as reasonably practicable after the end of the day\ndetermined under subsection 94Y(1), the data store administrator\nmust delete all COVID app data from the National COVIDSafe\nData Store.\n\n(3) As soon as reasonably practicable after the deletion, the data store\nadministrator must:\n\n(a) inform the Health Minister and the Commissioner that all\nCOVID app data has been deleted from the National\nCOVIDSafe Data Store; and\n\n(b) take all reasonable steps to inform all COVIDSafe users\n(other than former COVIDSafe users) in relation to\ncommunication devices that:\n\n(i) all COVID app data has been deleted from the National\nCOVIDSafe Data Store; and\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\n\nNo. 44, 2020\nPrivacy Amendment (Public Health Contact Information) Act 2020\n\n(ii) COVID app data can no longer be collected; and\n\n(iii) they should delete COVIDSafe from their\ncommunication devices.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-public-health-contact-information-act-2020-sch-1-sec-94p-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-public-health-contact-information-act-2020-sch-1-sec-94p-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-public-health-contact-information-act-2020-sch-1-sec-94p-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "60132efd10b022e0b71d14ca9be94235ad88e0e21f14ca685067ecdf402ea3c9"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-public-health-contact-information-act-2020#sch-1-sec-94p",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "94P Obligations after the end of the COVIDSafe data period",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 18,
      "values:originalText": "(1) After the end of the day determined under subsection 94Y(1), the\ndata store administrator must not:\n\n(a) collect any COVID app data; or\n\n(b) make COVIDSafe available to be downloaded.\n\n(2) As soon as reasonably practicable after the end of the day\ndetermined under subsection 94Y(1), the data store administrator\nmust delete all COVID app data from the National COVIDSafe\nData Store.\n\n(3) As soon as reasonably practicable after the deletion, the data store\nadministrator must:\n\n(a) inform the Health Minister and the Commissioner that all\nCOVID app data has been deleted from the National\nCOVIDSafe Data Store; and\n\n(b) take all reasonable steps to inform all COVIDSafe users\n(other than former COVIDSafe users) in relation to\ncommunication devices that:\n\n(i) all COVID app data has been deleted from the National\nCOVIDSafe Data Store; and\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\n\nNo. 44, 2020\nPrivacy Amendment (Public Health Contact Information) Act 2020\n\n(ii) COVID app data can no longer be collected; and\n\n(iii) they should delete COVIDSafe from their\ncommunication devices."
    },
