    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-public-health-contact-information-act-2020-sch-1-sec-94s-ss-5",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "94S(5) Breach of requirement may be treated as an eligible data breach",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-public-health-contact-information-act-2020#sch-1-sec-94s-ss-5"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-amendment-public-health-contact-information-act-2020.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-public-health-contact-information-act-2020.pdf, p.19",
      "values:originalText": "(5) The Commissioner may decide not to require compliance, or to\nallow an extended period for compliance, if the Commissioner is\nsatisfied on reasonable grounds that requiring compliance, or\nrequiring compliance within the ordinary period for compliance,\nwould not be reasonable in the circumstances, having regard to the\nfollowing:\n\n(a) the public interest;\n\n(b) any relevant advice given to the Commissioner by:\n\n(i) an enforcement body; or\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\n\nNo. 44, 2020\nPrivacy Amendment (Public Health Contact Information) Act 2020\n\n(ii) the Australian Signals Directorate;\n\n(c) such other matters (if any) as the Commissioner considers\nrelevant.",
      "skos:definition": "(5) The Commissioner may decide not to require compliance, or to\nallow an extended period for compliance, if the Commissioner is\nsatisfied on reasonable grounds that requiring compliance, or\nrequiring compliance within the ordinary period for compliance,\nwould not be reasonable in the circumstances, having regard to the\nfollowing:\n\n(a) the public interest;\n\n(b) any relevant advice given to the Commissioner by:\n\n(i) an enforcement body; or\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\n\nNo. 44, 2020\nPrivacy Amendment (Public Health Contact Information) Act 2020\n\n(ii) the Australian Signals Directorate;\n\n(c) such other matters (if any) as the Commissioner considers\nrelevant.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-public-health-contact-information-act-2020-sch-1-sec-94s"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-public-health-contact-information-act-2020-sch-1-sec-94s-ss-5-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "28895525b659033035015320a714ac5be4f132ba93e6fed0a3392f426ec245d2",
      "skos:note": "Commissioner may decide not to require compliance or allow extended period for compliance under certain circumstances."
    },
    {
