    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-public-health-contact-information-act-2020-sch-1-sec-94t",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "94T Commissioner may conduct an assessment relating to COVID",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-public-health-contact-information-act-2020#sch-1-sec-94t"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-amendment-public-health-contact-information-act-2020.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-public-health-contact-information-act-2020.pdf, p.21",
      "values:originalText": "app data\n\n(1) The Commissioner’s power under section 33C to conduct an\nassessment includes the power to conduct an assessment of\nwhether the acts or practices of an entity or a State or Territory\nauthority in relation to COVID app data comply with this Part.\n\n(2) Without limiting subsection 33C(2), if:\n\n(a) the Commissioner is conducting under that subsection an\nassessment of a matter of a kind mentioned in subsection (1)\nof this section; and\n\n(b) the Commissioner has reason to believe that an entity or a\nState or Territory authority being assessed has information or\na document relevant to the assessment;\nthe Commissioner may, by written notice, require the entity or\nauthority to give the information or produce the document within\nthe period specified in the notice, which must not be less than 14\ndays after the notice is given to the entity or authority.\nNote:\nFor a failure to give information etc., see section 66.",
      "skos:definition": "app data\n\n(1) The Commissioner’s power under section 33C to conduct an\nassessment includes the power to conduct an assessment of\nwhether the acts or practices of an entity or a State or Territory\nauthority in relation to COVID app data comply with this Part.\n\n(2) Without limiting subsection 33C(2), if:\n\n(a) the Commissioner is conducting under that subsection an\nassessment of a matter of a kind mentioned in subsection (1)\nof this section; and\n\n(b) the Commissioner has reason to believe that an entity or a\nState or Territory authority being assessed has information or\na document relevant to the assessment;\nthe Commissioner may, by written notice, require the entity or\nauthority to give the information or produce the document within\nthe period specified in the notice, which must not be less than 14\ndays after the notice is given to the entity or authority.\nNote:\nFor a failure to give information etc., see section 66.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-public-health-contact-information-act-2020-sch-1-sec-94t-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-public-health-contact-information-act-2020-sch-1-sec-94t-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "2e05d071615d86bed26a290f1c2e2569179b1565f5ea7a86d7f2b431dd3790a0"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-public-health-contact-information-act-2020#sch-1-sec-94t",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "94T Commissioner may conduct an assessment relating to COVID",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 21,
      "values:originalText": "app data\n\n(1) The Commissioner’s power under section 33C to conduct an\nassessment includes the power to conduct an assessment of\nwhether the acts or practices of an entity or a State or Territory\nauthority in relation to COVID app data comply with this Part.\n\n(2) Without limiting subsection 33C(2), if:\n\n(a) the Commissioner is conducting under that subsection an\nassessment of a matter of a kind mentioned in subsection (1)\nof this section; and\n\n(b) the Commissioner has reason to believe that an entity or a\nState or Territory authority being assessed has information or\na document relevant to the assessment;\nthe Commissioner may, by written notice, require the entity or\nauthority to give the information or produce the document within\nthe period specified in the notice, which must not be less than 14\ndays after the notice is given to the entity or authority.\nNote:\nFor a failure to give information etc., see section 66."
    },
