    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-public-health-contact-information-act-2020-sch-1-sec-94v",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "94V Referring COVID data matters to State or Territory privacy",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-public-health-contact-information-act-2020#sch-1-sec-94v"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-amendment-public-health-contact-information-act-2020.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-public-health-contact-information-act-2020.pdf, p.22",
      "values:originalText": "authorities\n\n(1) If:\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\n\nNo. 44, 2020\nPrivacy Amendment (Public Health Contact Information) Act 2020\n\n(a) a complaint has been made under section 36 about an act or\npractice that may involve a breach of a requirement of this\nPart; and\n\n(b) before the Commissioner commences, or after the\nCommissioner has commenced, to investigate the matter, the\nCommissioner forms the opinion that:\n\n(i) the complainant has made, or could have made, a\ncomplaint relating to that matter to a State or Territory\nprivacy authority; and\n\n(ii) that matter could be more conveniently or effectively\ndealt with by that State or Territory authority;\nthe Commissioner may decide not to investigate the matter, or not\nto investigate the matter further.\n\n(2) If the Commissioner so decides, the Commissioner must:\n\n(a) transfer the complaint to that State or Territory authority; and\n\n(b) give notice in writing to the complainant stating that the\ncomplaint has been so transferred; and\n\n(c) give to that State or Territory authority any information or\ndocuments that relate to the complaint and are in the\npossession, or under the control, of the Commissioner.\n\n(3) A complaint transferred under subsection (2) is taken, for the\npurposes of this Act, to have been made to that State or Territory\nauthority.",
      "skos:definition": "authorities\n\n(1) If:\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\n\nNo. 44, 2020\nPrivacy Amendment (Public Health Contact Information) Act 2020\n\n(a) a complaint has been made under section 36 about an act or\npractice that may involve a breach of a requirement of this\nPart; and\n\n(b) before the Commissioner commences, or after the\nCommissioner has commenced, to investigate the matter, the\nCommissioner forms the opinion that:\n\n(i) the complainant has made, or could have made, a\ncomplaint relating to that matter to a State or Territory\nprivacy authority; and\n\n(ii) that matter could be more conveniently or effectively\ndealt with by that State or Territory authority;\nthe Commissioner may decide not to investigate the matter, or not\nto investigate the matter further.\n\n(2) If the Commissioner so decides, the Commissioner must:\n\n(a) transfer the complaint to that State or Territory authority; and\n\n(b) give notice in writing to the complainant stating that the\ncomplaint has been so transferred; and\n\n(c) give to that State or Territory authority any information or\ndocuments that relate to the complaint and are in the\npossession, or under the control, of the Commissioner.\n\n(3) A complaint transferred under subsection (2) is taken, for the\npurposes of this Act, to have been made to that State or Territory\nauthority.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-public-health-contact-information-act-2020-sch-1-sec-94v-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-public-health-contact-information-act-2020-sch-1-sec-94v-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-public-health-contact-information-act-2020-sch-1-sec-94v-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "9756757b8c6dd29422388434c0fda529a4a8b5bc95d590808b958a1d60325117"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-public-health-contact-information-act-2020#sch-1-sec-94v",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "94V Referring COVID data matters to State or Territory privacy",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 22,
      "values:originalText": "authorities\n\n(1) If:\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\n\nNo. 44, 2020\nPrivacy Amendment (Public Health Contact Information) Act 2020\n\n(a) a complaint has been made under section 36 about an act or\npractice that may involve a breach of a requirement of this\nPart; and\n\n(b) before the Commissioner commences, or after the\nCommissioner has commenced, to investigate the matter, the\nCommissioner forms the opinion that:\n\n(i) the complainant has made, or could have made, a\ncomplaint relating to that matter to a State or Territory\nprivacy authority; and\n\n(ii) that matter could be more conveniently or effectively\ndealt with by that State or Territory authority;\nthe Commissioner may decide not to investigate the matter, or not\nto investigate the matter further.\n\n(2) If the Commissioner so decides, the Commissioner must:\n\n(a) transfer the complaint to that State or Territory authority; and\n\n(b) give notice in writing to the complainant stating that the\ncomplaint has been so transferred; and\n\n(c) give to that State or Territory authority any information or\ndocuments that relate to the complaint and are in the\npossession, or under the control, of the Commissioner.\n\n(3) A complaint transferred under subsection (2) is taken, for the\npurposes of this Act, to have been made to that State or Territory\nauthority."
    },
