      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(3) A complaint transferred under subsection (2) is taken, for the purposes of this Act, to have been made to that State or Territory authority.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The complaint is recognized by the relevant authority."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-public-health-contact-information-act-2020-sch-1-sec-94w",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "94W Commissioner may share information with State or Territory",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-public-health-contact-information-act-2020#sch-1-sec-94w"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-amendment-public-health-contact-information-act-2020.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-public-health-contact-information-act-2020.pdf, p.23",
      "values:originalText": "privacy authorities\n\n(1) Subject to subsection (2), the Commissioner may share information\nor documents with a State or Territory privacy authority:\n\n(a) for the purpose of the Commissioner exercising powers, or\nperforming functions or duties under this Act in relation to\nthe requirements of this Part; or\n\n(b) for the purpose of the State or Territory privacy authority\nexercising its powers, or performing its functions or duties.\n\n(2) The Commissioner may only share information or documents with\na State or Territory privacy authority under this section if:\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Public Health Contact Information) Act 2020\nNo. 44, 2020\n\n(a) the information or documents were acquired by the\nCommissioner in the course of exercising powers, or\nperforming functions or duties, under this Act; and\n\n(b) the Commissioner is satisfied on reasonable grounds that the\nState or Territory privacy authority has satisfactory\narrangements in place for protecting the information or\ndocuments.\n\n(3) To avoid doubt, the Commissioner may share information or\ndocuments with a State or Territory privacy authority under this\nsection whether or not the Commissioner is transferring a\ncomplaint or part of a complaint to the authority.",
      "skos:definition": "privacy authorities\n\n(1) Subject to subsection (2), the Commissioner may share information\nor documents with a State or Territory privacy authority:\n\n(a) for the purpose of the Commissioner exercising powers, or\nperforming functions or duties under this Act in relation to\nthe requirements of this Part; or\n\n(b) for the purpose of the State or Territory privacy authority\nexercising its powers, or performing its functions or duties.\n\n(2) The Commissioner may only share information or documents with\na State or Territory privacy authority under this section if:\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Public Health Contact Information) Act 2020\nNo. 44, 2020\n\n(a) the information or documents were acquired by the\nCommissioner in the course of exercising powers, or\nperforming functions or duties, under this Act; and\n\n(b) the Commissioner is satisfied on reasonable grounds that the\nState or Territory privacy authority has satisfactory\narrangements in place for protecting the information or\ndocuments.\n\n(3) To avoid doubt, the Commissioner may share information or\ndocuments with a State or Territory privacy authority under this\nsection whether or not the Commissioner is transferring a\ncomplaint or part of a complaint to the authority.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-public-health-contact-information-act-2020-sch-1-sec-94w-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-public-health-contact-information-act-2020-sch-1-sec-94w-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-public-health-contact-information-act-2020-sch-1-sec-94w-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "b6b3d6b9b0f51c850a7d3de373cad030d0ab89f687c25c6e255eaa13c4a00ba9"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-public-health-contact-information-act-2020#sch-1-sec-94w",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "94W Commissioner may share information with State or Territory",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 23,
      "values:originalText": "privacy authorities\n\n(1) Subject to subsection (2), the Commissioner may share information\nor documents with a State or Territory privacy authority:\n\n(a) for the purpose of the Commissioner exercising powers, or\nperforming functions or duties under this Act in relation to\nthe requirements of this Part; or\n\n(b) for the purpose of the State or Territory privacy authority\nexercising its powers, or performing its functions or duties.\n\n(2) The Commissioner may only share information or documents with\na State or Territory privacy authority under this section if:\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Public Health Contact Information) Act 2020\nNo. 44, 2020\n\n(a) the information or documents were acquired by the\nCommissioner in the course of exercising powers, or\nperforming functions or duties, under this Act; and\n\n(b) the Commissioner is satisfied on reasonable grounds that the\nState or Territory privacy authority has satisfactory\narrangements in place for protecting the information or\ndocuments.\n\n(3) To avoid doubt, the Commissioner may share information or\ndocuments with a State or Territory privacy authority under this\nsection whether or not the Commissioner is transferring a\ncomplaint or part of a complaint to the authority."
    },
