    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-public-health-contact-information-act-2020-sch-1-sec-94y",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "94Y Determining the end of the COVIDSafe data period",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-public-health-contact-information-act-2020#sch-1-sec-94y"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-amendment-public-health-contact-information-act-2020.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-public-health-contact-information-act-2020.pdf, p.24",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Subject to subsection (2), the Health Minister must, by notifiable\ninstrument, determine a day if the Health Minister is satisfied that,\nby that day, use of COVIDSafe:\n\n(a) is no longer required to prevent or control; or\n\n(b) is no longer likely to be effective in preventing or\ncontrolling;\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\n\nNo. 44, 2020\nPrivacy Amendment (Public Health Contact Information) Act 2020\n\nthe entry, emergence, establishment or spread of the coronavirus\nknown as COVID-19 into Australia or any part of Australia.\n\n(2) The Health Minister must not make a determination under\nsubsection (1) unless the Health Minister has consulted, or\nconsidered recommendations from, the Commonwealth Chief\nMedical Officer or the Australian Health Protection Principal\nCommittee.\n\n(3) The Commonwealth Chief Medical Officer or the Australian\nHealth Protection Principal Committee may recommend to the\nHealth Minister that the Health Minister make a determination\nunder subsection (1).",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Subject to subsection (2), the Health Minister must, by notifiable\ninstrument, determine a day if the Health Minister is satisfied that,\nby that day, use of COVIDSafe:\n\n(a) is no longer required to prevent or control; or\n\n(b) is no longer likely to be effective in preventing or\ncontrolling;\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\n\nNo. 44, 2020\nPrivacy Amendment (Public Health Contact Information) Act 2020\n\nthe entry, emergence, establishment or spread of the coronavirus\nknown as COVID-19 into Australia or any part of Australia.\n\n(2) The Health Minister must not make a determination under\nsubsection (1) unless the Health Minister has consulted, or\nconsidered recommendations from, the Commonwealth Chief\nMedical Officer or the Australian Health Protection Principal\nCommittee.\n\n(3) The Commonwealth Chief Medical Officer or the Australian\nHealth Protection Principal Committee may recommend to the\nHealth Minister that the Health Minister make a determination\nunder subsection (1).",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-public-health-contact-information-act-2020-sch-1-sec-94y-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-public-health-contact-information-act-2020-sch-1-sec-94y-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-public-health-contact-information-act-2020-sch-1-sec-94y-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "a05ef0d543fc2220e6a5efd12156be53b41b8d6865e96e976c96628d21c392ca"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-public-health-contact-information-act-2020#sch-1-sec-94y",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "94Y Determining the end of the COVIDSafe data period",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 24,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Subject to subsection (2), the Health Minister must, by notifiable\ninstrument, determine a day if the Health Minister is satisfied that,\nby that day, use of COVIDSafe:\n\n(a) is no longer required to prevent or control; or\n\n(b) is no longer likely to be effective in preventing or\ncontrolling;\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\n\nNo. 44, 2020\nPrivacy Amendment (Public Health Contact Information) Act 2020\n\nthe entry, emergence, establishment or spread of the coronavirus\nknown as COVID-19 into Australia or any part of Australia.\n\n(2) The Health Minister must not make a determination under\nsubsection (1) unless the Health Minister has consulted, or\nconsidered recommendations from, the Commonwealth Chief\nMedical Officer or the Australian Health Protection Principal\nCommittee.\n\n(3) The Commonwealth Chief Medical Officer or the Australian\nHealth Protection Principal Committee may recommend to the\nHealth Minister that the Health Minister make a determination\nunder subsection (1)."
    },
    {
