    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-public-health-contact-information-act-2020-sch-1-sec-94z",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "94Z Agencies may be determined to be data store administrator",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-public-health-contact-information-act-2020#sch-1-sec-94z"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-amendment-public-health-contact-information-act-2020.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-public-health-contact-information-act-2020.pdf, p.25",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Secretary of the Health Department may, by notifiable\ninstrument, determine that a particular agency is the data store\nadministrator for the purposes of one or more provisions of this\nPart specified in the determination.\n\n(2) The determination may limit the extent to which the agency is the\ndata store administrator for those purposes.\n\n(3) The Secretary of the Health Department must not determine under\nsubsection (1) that any of the following is the data store\nadministrator:\n\n(a) an enforcement body mentioned in paragraph (a) to (ea) of\nthe definition of enforcement body in subsection 6(1);\n\n(b) an intelligence agency;\n\n(c) the Australian Geospatial-Intelligence Organisation;\n\n(d) the Defence Intelligence Organisation.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Secretary of the Health Department may, by notifiable\ninstrument, determine that a particular agency is the data store\nadministrator for the purposes of one or more provisions of this\nPart specified in the determination.\n\n(2) The determination may limit the extent to which the agency is the\ndata store administrator for those purposes.\n\n(3) The Secretary of the Health Department must not determine under\nsubsection (1) that any of the following is the data store\nadministrator:\n\n(a) an enforcement body mentioned in paragraph (a) to (ea) of\nthe definition of enforcement body in subsection 6(1);\n\n(b) an intelligence agency;\n\n(c) the Australian Geospatial-Intelligence Organisation;\n\n(d) the Defence Intelligence Organisation.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-public-health-contact-information-act-2020-sch-1-sec-94z-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-public-health-contact-information-act-2020-sch-1-sec-94z-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-public-health-contact-information-act-2020-sch-1-sec-94z-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "24d24723ae13b6b4d4567a5d1f5e1dfa8fd5de630447610faa0a806b974d7db7"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-public-health-contact-information-act-2020#sch-1-sec-94z",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "94Z Agencies may be determined to be data store administrator",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 25,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Secretary of the Health Department may, by notifiable\ninstrument, determine that a particular agency is the data store\nadministrator for the purposes of one or more provisions of this\nPart specified in the determination.\n\n(2) The determination may limit the extent to which the agency is the\ndata store administrator for those purposes.\n\n(3) The Secretary of the Health Department must not determine under\nsubsection (1) that any of the following is the data store\nadministrator:\n\n(a) an enforcement body mentioned in paragraph (a) to (ea) of\nthe definition of enforcement body in subsection 6(1);\n\n(b) an intelligence agency;\n\n(c) the Australian Geospatial-Intelligence Organisation;\n\n(d) the Defence Intelligence Organisation."
    },
