    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-public-health-contact-information-act-2020-sch-1-sec-94za",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "94ZA Reports on operation and effectiveness of COVIDSafe and the",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-public-health-contact-information-act-2020#sch-1-sec-94za"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-amendment-public-health-contact-information-act-2020.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-public-health-contact-information-act-2020.pdf, p.25",
      "values:originalText": "National COVIDSafe Data Store\n\n(1) The Health Minister must, as soon as practicable after:\n\n(a) the end of the 6 month period starting on the commencement\nof this Part; and\n\n(b) the end of each subsequent 6 month period (if any) starting\non or before the day determined under subsection 94Y(1);\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Public Health Contact Information) Act 2020\nNo. 44, 2020\n\ncause a report to be prepared on the operation and effectiveness of\nCOVIDSafe and the National COVIDSafe Data Store during that 6\nmonth period.\nNote:\nSection 94D prevents the inclusion of COVID app data in the report.\nIt would not be a permitted collection, use or disclosure under\nsubsection 94D(2).\n\n(2) If the day determined under subsection 94Y(1) occurs during the 6\nmonth period starting on the commencement of this Part, the report\nunder subsection (1) of this section relating to that period must be\nprepared within 3 months after that day.\n\n(3) The Health Minister must cause copies of a report prepared under\nsubsection (1) to be laid before each House of the Parliament\nwithin 15 sitting days of that House after the completion of the\npreparation of the report.",
      "skos:definition": "National COVIDSafe Data Store\n\n(1) The Health Minister must, as soon as practicable after:\n\n(a) the end of the 6 month period starting on the commencement\nof this Part; and\n\n(b) the end of each subsequent 6 month period (if any) starting\non or before the day determined under subsection 94Y(1);\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Public Health Contact Information) Act 2020\nNo. 44, 2020\n\ncause a report to be prepared on the operation and effectiveness of\nCOVIDSafe and the National COVIDSafe Data Store during that 6\nmonth period.\nNote:\nSection 94D prevents the inclusion of COVID app data in the report.\nIt would not be a permitted collection, use or disclosure under\nsubsection 94D(2).\n\n(2) If the day determined under subsection 94Y(1) occurs during the 6\nmonth period starting on the commencement of this Part, the report\nunder subsection (1) of this section relating to that period must be\nprepared within 3 months after that day.\n\n(3) The Health Minister must cause copies of a report prepared under\nsubsection (1) to be laid before each House of the Parliament\nwithin 15 sitting days of that House after the completion of the\npreparation of the report.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-public-health-contact-information-act-2020-sch-1-sec-94za-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-public-health-contact-information-act-2020-sch-1-sec-94za-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-public-health-contact-information-act-2020-sch-1-sec-94za-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "41ec30cdf725a17bffa428994ae0a79d6406794343ba7cc7afbc5e6bbe500138"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-public-health-contact-information-act-2020#sch-1-sec-94za",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "94ZA Reports on operation and effectiveness of COVIDSafe and the",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 25,
      "values:originalText": "National COVIDSafe Data Store\n\n(1) The Health Minister must, as soon as practicable after:\n\n(a) the end of the 6 month period starting on the commencement\nof this Part; and\n\n(b) the end of each subsequent 6 month period (if any) starting\non or before the day determined under subsection 94Y(1);\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments\n\nPrivacy Amendment (Public Health Contact Information) Act 2020\nNo. 44, 2020\n\ncause a report to be prepared on the operation and effectiveness of\nCOVIDSafe and the National COVIDSafe Data Store during that 6\nmonth period.\nNote:\nSection 94D prevents the inclusion of COVID app data in the report.\nIt would not be a permitted collection, use or disclosure under\nsubsection 94D(2).\n\n(2) If the day determined under subsection 94Y(1) occurs during the 6\nmonth period starting on the commencement of this Part, the report\nunder subsection (1) of this section relating to that period must be\nprepared within 3 months after that day.\n\n(3) The Health Minister must cause copies of a report prepared under\nsubsection (1) to be laid before each House of the Parliament\nwithin 15 sitting days of that House after the completion of the\npreparation of the report."
    },
